  "notes": {
    "include-search": "Quoted includes search the including file's own directory first, then the -I directories (CMake target_include_directories: include/). So `#include \"inventory.h\"` from src/ is include/inventory.h, `\"conn.h\"` from src/net/ is src/net/conn.h, `\"net/conn.h\"` and `\"report.h\"` from src/main.cpp are src/net/conn.h and src/report.h, `\"platform.h\"` from src/net/ is include/platform.h. Angle-bracket system headers are external.",
    "two-log-h": "There are two log.h files, include/util/log.h (util::log_info) and src/net/log.h (net::log_info). src/net/conn.cpp's `#include \"log.h\"` finds src/net/log.h first (own directory), and its unqualified log_info inside namespace net is net::log_info. src/main.cpp and src/inventory.cpp include \"util/log.h\", which does not exist under src/ so comes from include/, and call util::log_info.",
    "header-plus-source": "Member functions declared in a header (include/inventory.h, include/util/strings.h, src/report.h) are defined in the same-stem source file; the call target is the definition (src/inventory.cpp, src/util/strings.cpp, src/report.cpp), not the declaring header.",
    "inline-in-header": "Inventory::size is defined inline in include/inventory.h, so the header is the target.",
    "platform-variants": "now_ms is declared in include/platform.h and defined in both platform_posix.cpp and platform_win.cpp; CMake compiles exactly one depending on WIN32. Ambiguous at file granularity.",
    "stl-self-name": "`items_.size()` inside Inventory::size is std::vector::size: must not become a self-loop.",
    "stl-find": "`std::find(...)` in known() is the STL algorithm, not Inventory::find.",
    "imports-format": "IMPORTS rows are quoted #include directives resolved to an in-repo file by the search rule above, kind `include`.",
    "scope": "Constructors (`net::Connection conn(...)`, `Inventory inv;`) are not listed as calls. Calls inside lambdas are not listed."
  }
